subject: fix(custom-server): always log warn when L1 settings load gives up (GAP-P2-34)

The L1 peer-forwarding settings loader retries 10 times with exponential
backoff but previously only logged the give-up message when DEBUG_L1_PEER_FORWARD
was set. Production deployments with misconfigured peer nodes got no L1
forwarding with no indication.

Now: console.warn fires unconditionally after 10 failed attempts so operators
always know peer forwarding is disabled. The detailed error message stays
DEBUG-gated to avoid log spam.

Adds behavioral test documenting the expected retry/warn boundary.

